 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Earth Manipulation — Innate Technique (18th level)</em></p><p><em>Domain Expansion (rules): full-turn action, 20 CE unless stated, 175-ft radius, 1 minute. When the domain ends you suffer <strong>Technique Burnout</strong> (applied automatically by the module).</em></p><p>At 18th level you have learned to expand your domain. At initiative 20, all creatures of your choice within your domain take 6d12 bludgeoning damage and are restrained by shifting stone until the start of their next turn.<br />\nYou can spend an action to change the environment of your domain. </p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>You can create a large 20 ft radius, 1d10 x 10 feet deep chasm causing creatures to fall and take falling damage.   </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You can create a 100 ft tall tower of stone (as if casting Galdur’s Tower with 10 stories).  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You can create 100 ft of difficult terrain in an area you can see. A creature that moves through this area takes 2d4 piercing damage for every 5 feet moved.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
